section: linker
synopsis:
  The runtime's generic apply code (the ``stg_ap_*`` entry points) is no longer
  part of the RTS library; GHC generates and links it into every program, and
  into shared and static libraries that contain the RTS.
issues: #24347
mrs: !0
description: {
  Programs and libraries linked by GHC need no changes.  A Haskell shared
  library that is loaded by a program GHC did not link must now be built with
  ``-flink-rts``, or the generic apply code must be generated with the new
  ``ghc --gen-apply`` mode and added to the final link by hand; see the new
  "Linking the runtime's generic apply code" section of the users guide.  The
  new ``-fno-link-autoapply`` flag stops GHC from adding the code to a link.
  The standalone ``genapply`` build tool has been removed.
}
